Verse 1:
[C]O Thou in whose presence [F]my [C]soul [G7]takes de[C]light, On [Am]whom in [G7]af[C]flic[D7]tion I [G]call,
[C]My comfort [G]by [C]day and my [F]song [C]in the [G]night, [C]My hope, my [Am]sal[C]va[G7]tion, my [C]all!

Verse 2:
[C][F]His [C]voice, [G7]as [C]the [Am]sound [G7]of [C]the [D7]dulcimer [G]sweet,
[C][G]Is [C][F]heard [C]through [G][C]the [Am]shadows [C][G7]of [C]death;
[C][F]The [C]cedars [G7]of [C]Lebanon [Am][G7]bow [C]at [D7]His [G]feet,
[C][G]The [C][F]air [C]is [G][C]perfumed [Am]with [C][G7]His [C]breath.

Verse 3:
[C][F]His [C]lips, [G7]as [C]a [Am][G7]fountain [C]of [D7]righteousness [G]flow,
[C][G]To [C][F]water [C][G]the [C][Am]gardens [C][G7]of [C]grace;
[C][F]From [C]which [G7]their [C]salvation [Am][G7]the [C]Gentiles [D7]shall [G]know,
[C][G]And [C]bask [F][C]in [G]the [C]smiles [Am][C]of [G7]His [C]face.

Verse 4:
[C][F]He [C]looks, [G7]and [C]ten [Am][G7]thousands [C]of [D7]angels [G]rejoice,
[C][G]And [C][F]myriads [C][G]wait [C][Am]for [C][G7]His [C]word;
[C][F]He [C]speaks, [G7]and [C]eternity, [Am][G7]filled [C]with [D7]His [G]voice,
[C][G]Re-echoes [C][F]the [C][G]praise [C][Am]of [C][G7]the [C]Lord.
